# ─── CrewWatch kit upstream checkout: reference only, never committed ────────
# A clone of github.com/mateusands/claude-code-crew-kit, kept here to diff what
# .claude/ has against what upstream ships. It is someone else's repository
# with its own history — it must never become part of this one.
crewkit/

# ─── Vendor binaries: proprietary, never committed ───────────────────────────
# Husky's Windows app, kept locally as the reference behind docs/PROTOCOL.md's
# "A second vendor source". This rule is deliberately SEPARATE from the docs/
# entry below: docs/PROTOCOL.md is this project's declared source of truth and
# the README links to it six times, so docs/ ought to be published one day —
# and when it is, these binaries must not go with it.
docs/vendor-binaries/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.github/
docs/

# capture traffic never enters the repo
*.pcapng
*.pcap

# personal backups made with `open-ek75 backup`
backup*.json

# Your roster and your models — never committed (see .crew-kit-config.example)
.crew-kit-config

# ─── CrewWatch: the whole kit stays out of git ────────────────────────────────
# Everything the installer put here is tooling for whoever is driving the agent,
# not part of open-ek75. None of it is versioned, by decision.
#
# 🔴 Because nothing is distributed, nothing needs the MIT notice to travel with
# it. `.claude/LICENSE-crewwatch` is ignored along with the rest — that is the
# kit's own rule for a fully ignored install, not an oversight. Un-ignore the
# notice the day any of these files starts being committed.
.claude/
.crew/
.crew-kit-config.example
AGENTS.md
START.md
# CLAUDE.md here predates the kit — 107 lines of this project's own conventions,
# not an installed file. Ignored by decision: it stays on disk and out of git.
CLAUDE.md
.mcp.json
.mcp.json.example
.github/pull_request_template.md
